From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:14:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: accept ARGB8888 on the primary plane

The primary plane offered only XRGB8888. A GBM client whose EGL config
has alpha, such as glmark2-es2-drm on Zink, gets an ARGB8888 surface,
and its modeset failed with "Invalid pixel format AR24" before any
request reached the device. The driver already creates ARGB8888
framebuffers and translates the format to B8G8R8A8_UNORM for
SET_SCANOUT_BLOB, so the plane now lists it too. XRGB8888 stays first,
so fbdev and clients that take the first format keep it.

The plane has no blend-mode property, so DRM assumes premultiplied
alpha. A premultiplied pixel over the CRTC's black background shows
exactly its colour channels. That is what the Darwin host presents: it
ignores the fourth byte of a scanout, as it does for B8G8R8X8.

The other 32-bit RGB orders Android's composer scans out are a separate
option, DRM_VIRTIO_GPU_STANDARD_FORMATS, because they change which format
a Linux compositor picks.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
index 192327723bb9ad1e40c6742f5afa363498311fea..a3bab2b277934d74dc78672d11eb93f99d00c39a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 
 static const uint32_t virtio_gpu_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_HOST_XRGB8888,
+	DRM_FORMAT_HOST_ARGB8888,
 };
 
 static const uint32_t virtio_gpu_cursor_formats[] = {
